backtrack-ledger
===============

This distribution is a derivative work of regexp-tree.

Upstream
--------
regexp-tree
https://github.com/DmitrySoshnikov/regexp-tree
Copyright (c) 2017 Dmitry Soshnikov
Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

The parser, AST specification, generator, traversal API, transform pipeline,
optimizer and the finite-automaton interpreter are upstream code, used here
without modification except where noted below.

Modifications in this distribution
----------------------------------
1. `src/backtrack/` is new. It contains a backtracking virtual machine with an
   explicit choice stack, a compiler from the upstream AST to that machine's
   instruction set, capability analysis, attack-string construction, a cost
   ledger, and rewrite verification. Copyright (c) 2026 backtrack-ledger
   contributors, MIT.

2. `src/regexp-tree.js` gains one additive export, `backtrack`. No existing
   export changed.

3. `src/backtrack/__tests__/backtrack-test.js` is new (61 tests). The upstream
   test suite (398 tests) is unmodified.

4. `scripts/build.js` is modified to fix a cross-platform defect: the previous
   implementation invoked `NODE_ENV=production "node_modules/.bin/babel"`,
   which cannot run under cmd.exe, and exited 0 without producing `dist/`.
   The fix passes NODE_ENV through the child environment, tolerates git-hook
   symlink failure (which requires elevation on Windows), and fails loudly when
   `dist/regexp-tree.js` is absent. Reported upstream as issue #134.

5. `scripts/bundle-demo.js`, `scripts/verify-demo.js`, `scripts/png-probe.js`
   and `demo/` are new: a dependency-free browser bundle of the above, a
   headless DOM acceptance harness, and a PNG statistics probe used to verify
   that rendered pages are not blank.

6. `README.md` was replaced with documentation for this derivative work. The
   upstream README is preserved verbatim as `README.upstream.md`.

7. `bin/backtrack-ledger` is new. `bin/regexp-tree` is unchanged.

No upstream file was relicensed. The MIT terms in LICENSE apply to the whole
distribution.
